{title: Sent From The Heart Of God}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

>Lyrics

Introduction

Verse 1

Sent from the heart of God

Into the world of men,

Bringing Light to our darkened souls,

Giving life that will never end.

Leaving His royal throne,

Born as a lowly child,

Jesus came, giving all He had,

That our souls may be reconciled.

Chorus

Tell the world: He has come --

Our Savior, our Messiah!

By the wonder of His great plan,

Through His grace we are redeemed!

Spread the news: He has come --

Our Savior, our Messiah!

Turn your heart to receive Him now,

Jesus Christ, the King of kings!

Verse 2

Shepherds who saw the star

Came to behold their King.

Oh, the wonders they saw that night

When they heard the angels sing:

"Glory to God above,

Peace and goodwill to men".

Jesus opened the door to heav'n

That we all may enter in.

(Repeat Chorus)

Tell the world: He has come --

Our Savior, our Messiah!

By the wonder of His great plan,

Through His grace we are redeemed!

Spread the news: He has come --

Our Savior, our Messiah!

Turn your heart to receive Him now,

Jesus Christ, the King of kings!

(Repeat Chorus Again)

Tell the world: He has come --

Our Savior, our Messiah!

By the wonder of His great plan,

Through His grace we are redeemed!

Spread the news: He has come --

Our Savior, our Messiah!

Turn your heart to receive Him now,

Jesus Christ, the King of kings!

Turn your heart to receive Him now,

Jesus Christ, the King of kings!

Turn your heart to receive Him now,

Jesus Christ, the King of kings!
